{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793021677,"nonce":"hZ67s9z/F0Ydbm3ngHbf4UwL5NI=","message":"Implemented in b1be256 (Add recovery-preserving workspace reopen action).\n\nThe Warning toast now has a Reopen Workspace footer action. Notification cards use full-width wrapping text with separate icon/dismiss controls, right-aligned footer actions and status-bar clearance. Warning colors still come from the theme. This replaces the cramped layout where the button and message competed for the same row.\n\nThe action checkpoints dirty personal history, asynchronously asks the local page bridge to reopen, commits each existing document replica into its original IndexedDB namespace, waits for pending personal storage transactions, and reloads the same URL. A fresh authenticated handshake establishes the new context without migrating the old replica across the recovery fence. Checkpoint/storage failure or a bounded timeout keeps the page open and returns a retryable warning. Late checkpoint completion after timeout cannot navigate. No synchronous remote wait is added to the UI.\n\nValidation: all 37 browser session tests passed, including checkpoint ordering, storage failure and late timeout completion. Haxe SessionEditorChecks passed, including page.reopen over the bridge after the remote session disconnects. ToastLayout passed geometry/action checks and rendered Warning/Destructive cards in dark/light themes into bin/session-reopen-toast-layout without changing tracked snapshots. Two full WASM editors passed edit/undo/Save/reconnect/reload/fencing checks. The actual footer button click reloaded the same URL, preserved an offline old-workspace draft in its original IndexedDB cache, opened the replacement session and accepted new edits without replaying the old draft or raising a runtime error. Screenshots: bin/web/crdt-shots/a-replacement-blocked.png and a-reopened.png.\n\nWASM and native session rebuilt. The current local server was initially still serving the previous layout during user testing; the corrected bundle is now staged at bin/web/rayde, and HTTP-served hashes were verified against the tested build. WASM 6bd50e26d6c630fa113e6119418ad2a7afd6b4e1059c8865d3e6e0201d5b7d45, adapter 51df1406f7e3ad6bdf098d183883602c3116659358d8b5cda48aa25f52b2ac79. Session restarted at 127.0.0.1:7070 with existing URL/credentials/workspace/environment preserved. Refresh the current browser tab to load it. No push or deployment.","files":null}]}